## Context

Observed 2026-10-31, raid 8ad75a, PR 2073 (review rv-20261031-pr-2073-6e61).
The gaze seat `cx` ran on Codex: rollout
`~/.codex/sessions/2026/10/31/rollout-2026-10-31T10-57-59-01a19165-...jsonl`
(started 09:57:59Z) carries `"model_provider":"openai"`, `"model":"gpt-6.1-sol"`,
and the seat's own header said runtime=codex, family=openai, door=headless.
gaze_close nevertheless wrote the answer's reviewer line as

    reviewer: step=review · seat=cx · runtime=claude-code · model=anthropic/gpt-6.1-sol · ... · route=subagent

and verify-gate read both seats as family=anthropic (same-family review),
so a real cross-family seat was counted as same-family. The wrong line is
now in `memory/evidence/attribution/2026-10-31-review-attribution-pr2073.md`.
Cause not yet established (plan text named the seat openai; the close
step derived runtime/family elsewhere).

Severity: corrupts attribution state and can make a high-risk gate refuse a
review that has its cross-family seat.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Test: a gaze answer for a seat launched through the codex headless door
      records `runtime=codex`, `model=openai/<id>` and its door route
- [ ] The PR 2073 attribution record is corrected or annotated by a linked entry

